<%= form_with model: entry, url: entry.persisted? ? entry_path(entry) : entries_path, class: "book-form", data: { controller: "kind-switch" } do |f| %>
  <%= render "book_entries/errors", entry: entry %>
  <%= render "book_entries/identity_fields", f: f %>
  <div class="field-row">
    <div class="field">
      <%= f.label :kind %>
      <%= f.select :kind, GeneratorTable::KINDS.keys.map { |k| [ k.humanize, k ] }, {}, data: { kind_switch_target: "select", action: "kind-switch#update" } %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%# Lore is drawn evenly: its tables have no weights. %>
  <% show_for = ->(field) { GeneratorTable::KINDS.select { |kind, fields| (field == "weight" && GeneratorTable::LORE_KINDS.exclude?(kind)) || fields.include?(field) }.keys.join(" ") } %>
  <% columns = { "text" => "Text", "key" => "Key", "item" => "Item", "gil" => word("currency").upcase_first, "service" => "Service", "width" => "Width", "height" => "Height", "roof" => "Roof",
                 "makes" => "Makes (commas)", "rooms" => "Rooms (commas)", "heart" => "Heart", "keeps" => "Keeps (commas)", "named" => "Named (commas)",
                 "did" => "Did", "sealed" => "Left", "trace" => "What's still there", "dead" => "Who died there", "town" => "In a town (%s)",
                 "when" => "When it fits", "sets" => "What it remembers", "does" => "What it takes", "choices" => "The choice", "weight" => "Weight" } %>
  <% lore_columns = %w[makes rooms heart keeps named did sealed trace dead town when sets does choices] %>
  <fieldset class="panel">
    <legend>Rows</legend>
    <p class="hint" data-show-for="treasure">Each row is an item or an amount of <%= word("currency") %>.</p>
    <p class="hint" data-show-for="<%= GeneratorTable::LORE_KINDS.join(' ') %>">This is the world's lore: what its pocket history and the pasts of its places are made of. A world with none of a kind has none of that happen (no feuds without quarrels, no fallen dungeons without falls).</p>
    <p class="hint" data-show-for="forks">A fork's costly way can take something the first time the party goes that way. Write it in brackets after the text, as a thing to do's are: <code>pay 100</code> in <%= word("currency") %>, a number of parts of the day, <code>hurt 10</code> (a share of everyone's <%= word("hp") %>), <code>weary 25</code> (of their <%= word("mp") %>), or <code>ambush</code> (a fight from the place's encounter table). Without brackets, it's a cost the GM plays out.</p>
    <p class="hint" data-show-for="<%= GeneratorTable::STORY_KINDS.join(' ') %>">The row that fits the moment best is offered to the GM to say or skip (an arrival line on each arrival, complications when a check fails): the one asking the most of it wins, and a row that asks nothing is the fallback.
      <strong>When it fits</strong> is facts with commas (<code>town, night, !smoke_seen, hurt >= 2</code>); <strong>what it remembers</strong> is flags it sets once said
      (<code>smoke_seen, visits + 1</code>), so rows can rule each other out. <code>{place}</code> in the text says a fact; <code>{cold|still}</code> picks one.
      A row that names one of a table's lines or veils never comes up. <%= link_to "Every fact a row can ask about", world_generation_facts_path(@world) %>.</p>
    <p class="hint" data-show-for="complications">When a check fails, the GM is offered two moves, each the row that fits best: a <strong>soft</strong> one (a row that takes nothing: signs of trouble coming, an unwelcome truth, an opportunity at a cost) and a <strong>hard</strong> one, which takes something once the GM makes it so:
      <%= safe_join(Outcome::TAKES.map { |kind| tag.code(Outcome.of(kind).to_s) }, ", ") %>. A hard move with nothing to take (no clock running, an empty purse) isn't offered.
      A complication can also ask about the check: <code>who</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>stat</code>, <code>skill</code>, <code>move</code>, <code>difficulty</code>.</p>
    <p class="hint" data-show-for="events">When the party rests or travels (without a fight on the road), the event that fits best is offered to the GM, who can put it to the table. Its <strong>choice</strong> is options with <code>|</code> between them, each with what it does after a colon, and the flag the answer sets after <code>-&gt;</code>:
      <code>Share the fire: give potion, rumour | Send her off: tick -&gt; shared_fire</code>. Make each option cost something the table values against the other, not just HP against money.
      An option that can't happen now (nothing in the bag to give) drops out; an event left with fewer than two isn't offered. An event can ask <code>rest</code>, <code>camp</code>, <code>inn</code>, <code>road</code>, <code>to</code>, and the party's <code>hurt_one</code>, <code>tied</code>, <code>tied_to</code> and <code>from_&lt;origin&gt;</code>.</p>
    <p class="hint" data-show-for="locks">Each row is a lock and the key that opens it, in any flavour: Portal and Blue crystal, Altar and Goat's skull.</p>
    <p class="hint"><strong>Worlds are live:</strong> towns and dungeons already rolled from this table change with it, except the people and rooms a GM has pinned.</p>
    <p class="hint" data-show-for="<%= show_for.("weight") %>">Weight defaults to 1: a row with weight 3 comes up three times as often.</p>
    <p class="hint">Clear a row to remove it.</p>
    <% items = @world.items.order(:name).map { |i| [ i.name, i.slug ] } %>
    <table class="grid-form">
      <thead><tr><% columns.each do |key, label| %><th data-show-for="<%= show_for.(key) %>"><%= label %></th><% end %></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% rows_with_blanks(entry.entries, blanks: 3).each_with_index do |row, i| %>
          <% name = ->(key) { json_field_name(f, :entries, i, key) } %>
          <tr>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("text") %>"><%= text_field_tag name.(:text), row["text"], "aria-label": "Text #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("key") %>"><%= text_field_tag name.(:key), row["key"], "aria-label": "Key #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("item") %>"><%= select_tag name.(:item), options_for_select(items, row["item"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Item #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("gil") %>"><%= number_field_tag name.(:gil), row["gil"], min: 1, "aria-label": "Gil #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("service") %>"><%= select_tag name.(:service), options_for_select(Generators::Town::SERVICES.map { |s| [ s.humanize, s ] }, row["service"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Service #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("width") %>"><%= number_field_tag name.(:width), row["width"], min: 1, "aria-label": "Width #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("height") %>"><%= number_field_tag name.(:height), row["height"], min: 1, "aria-label": "Height #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("roof") %>"><%= select_tag name.(:roof), options_for_select(Generators::Town::ROOFS.map { |r| [ r.humanize, r ] }, row["roof"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Roof #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <% lore_columns.each do |key| %>
              <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.(key) %>"><%= text_field_tag name.(key), row[key], "aria-label": "#{columns[key]} #{i + 1}" %></td>
            <% end %>
            <td data-show-for="<%= show_for.("weight") %>"><%= number_field_tag name.(:weight), row["weight"], min: 1, placeholder: 1, "aria-label": "Weight #{i + 1}" %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <% pasteable = GeneratorTable::PASTE_FORMATS %>
    <div class="field" data-show-for="<%= pasteable.keys.join(' ') %>">
      <%= f.label :paste, "Add many at once" %>
      <%= f.text_area :paste, rows: 6, value: entry.paste %>
      <% pasteable.each do |kind, format| %>
        <p class="hint" data-show-for="<%= kind %>">One per line: <%= format %>.<% unless GeneratorTable::LORE_KINDS.include?(kind) %> Add <code>| 3</code> at the end of a line for a weight.<% end %></p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </fieldset>
  <div class="actions">
    <%= f.submit class: "button" %>
    <%= link_to "Cancel", entry.persisted? ? entry_path(entry) : entries_path, class: "button button--quiet" %>
  </div>
<% end %>
